:\"docs-prose\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L2a\",null,{\"title\":\"Using agent memory\",\"description\":\"Give your agents persistent memory that survives across sessions using memory stores.\",\"actions\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[false,[\"$\",\"$L2b\",null,{\"servedLocale\":\"en\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"data-not-prose\":true,\"className\":\"mt-0 mb-lg lg:hidden\",\"children\":\"$20:1:1:props:children:1:props:children:0:props:children:0:props:actions\"}],null,null,null,[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Each Managed Agents session starts with a fresh context by default. When a session ends, any state the agent built up is gone. Memory stores let the agent carry information across sessions: user preferences, project conventions, prior mistakes, and domain context.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L2c\",\"2\",{\"variant\":\"muted\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"prose-block [.prose_\u0026]:text-prose\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Managed Agents API requests require the \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"managed-agents-2026-04-01\"]}],\" beta header, except memory store endpoints, which use \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"agent-memory-2026-07-22\"]}],\" instead. The SDK sets the correct beta header automatically. See \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/api/beta-headers#endpoint-specific-headers\",\"children\":[\"Beta headers\"]}],\".\"]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L2c\",\"4\",{\"variant\":\"muted\",\"id\":\"$undefined\",\"icon\":\"$undefined\",\"className\":\"prose-block [.prose_\u0026]:text-prose\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Don't combine \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"agent-memory-2026-07-22\"]}],\" with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"managed-agents-2026-04-01\"]}],\" on a memory store request: sending both returns a \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"400\"]}],\" error. If your code sets beta headers explicitly, replace \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"managed-agents-2026-04-01\"]}],\" with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"9\",{\"children\":[\"agent-memory-2026-07-22\"]}],\" on memory store calls rather than adding a second value. Session endpoints, including attaching a memory store to a session, still use \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"11\",{\"children\":[\"managed-agents-2026-04-01\"]}],\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"code\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"GET /v1/memory_stores/{memory_store_id}/memories\"]}],\" behaves the same under either header: results come back in a stable, server-defined order, and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"path_prefix\"]}],\" and \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"4\",{\"children\":[\"depth\"]}],\" apply the same way.\"]}]]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"$L2e\",\"6\",{\"level\":2,\"slug\":\"overview\",\"children\":[\"Overview\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"8\",{\"children\":[\"A \",[\"$\",\"strong\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"memory store\"]}],\" is a workspace-scoped collection of text documents optimized for Claude. When you attach a store to a session, it is mounted as a directory inside the session's sandbox. The agent reads and writes it with the same file tools it uses for the rest of the filesystem, and a note describing each mount is automatically added to the system prompt, telling the agent where to look. The \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",\"3\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/tools\",\"children\":[\"agent toolset\"]}],\" is required for these interactions; make sure to enable it during \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",\"5\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/agent-setup\",\"children\":[\"agent creation\"]}],\". On \",\"$L2f\",\", that directory is not a live mount. Instead, the SDK's environment worker downloads each attached store into your sandbox before the agent's tools run and keeps that copy in sync with the store.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$L30\",\"\\n\",\"$L31\",\"\\n\",\"$L32\",\"\\n\",\"$L33\",\"\\n\",\"$L34\",\"\\n\",\"$L35\",\"\\n\",\"$L36\",\"\\n\",\"$L37\",\"\\n\",\"$L38\",\"\\n\",\"$L39\",\"\\n\",\"$L3a\",\"\\n\",\"$L3b\",\"\\n\",\"$L3c\",\"\\n\",\"$L3d\",\"\\n\",\"\\n\",\"$L3e\",\"\\n\",\"$L3f\",\"\\n\",\"$L40\",\"\\n\",\"$L41\",\"\\n\",\"$L42\",\"\\n\",\"$L43\",\"\\n\",\"$L44\",\"\\n\",\"$L45\",\"\\n\",\"$L46\",\"\\n\",\"$L47\",\"\\n\",\"$L48\",\"\\n\",\"$L49\",\"\\n\",\"$L4a\",\"\\n\",\"$L4b\",\"\\n\",\"$L4c\",\"\\n\",\"$L4d\",\"\\n\",\"$L4e\",\"\\n\",\"$L4f\",\"\\n\",\"$L50\",\"\\n\",\"$L51\",\"\\n\",\"$L52\",\"\\n\",\"$L53\",\"\\n\",\"$L54\",\"\\n\",\"$L55\",\"\\n\",\"$L56\",\"\\n\",\"$L57\",\"\\n\",\"$L58\",\"\\n\",\"$L59\",\"\\n\",\"$L5a\",\"\\n\",\"$L5b\",\"\\n\",\"$L5c\",\"\\n\",\"$L5d\",\"\\n\",\"$L5e\",\"\\n\",\"$L5f\",\"\\n\",\"$L60\",\"\\n\",\"$L61\",\"\\n\",\"$L62\",\"\\n\",\"$L63\",\"\\n\",\"$L64\",\"\\n\",\"$L65\",\"\\n\",\"$L66\",\"\\n\",\"$L67\",\"\\n\",\"$L68\",\"\\n\",\"$L69\",\"\\n\",\"$L6a\",\"\\n\",\"$L6b\",\"\\n\",\"$L6c\",\"\\n\",\"$L6d\",\"\\n\",\"$L6e\",\"\\n\",\"$L6f\",\"\\n\",\"$L70\",\"\\n\",\"$L71\",\"\\n\",\"$L72\",\"\\n\",\"$L73\",\"\\n\",\"$L74\",\"\\n\",\"$L75\",\"\\n\",\"$L76\",\"\\n\",\"$L77\",\"\\n\",\"$L78\",\"\\n\",\"$L79\",\"\\n\",\"$L7a\",\"\\n\",\"$L7b\",\"\\n\",\"$L7c\",\"\\n\",\"$L7d\",\"\\n\",\"$L7e\",\"\\n\",\"$L7f\"],null]}],\"$L80\"]}],\"$L81\"]}],\"$L82\",\"$L83\",null]]\n84:I[850034,[\"/_next/static/chunks/3k2m7vl-q_yuf.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/1pj26-7691n-t.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0zmavsunzk_k0.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/12zccx4oz30ml.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/1k_y-k_13m45r.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2nxnebntv2rsq.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2u2-784egu1jl.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0rrx5prb_wy1f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0k_snsjvai8lo.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/17jen4dztv5y6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/1wshgyk2i870c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/271dt6fdljpdw.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0w2qk13qp6q2f.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2g4n97xdbriie.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2t103nzz143qn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2vjhhd4yekh7j.js\",\"/_next/static/chunk