lls and the agent's file writes to unmapped paths. Existing memories remain readable and editable. The following practices help you stay well under the limit and recover gracefully if you reach it.\"]}]\n7f:[\"$\",\"ul\",\"169\",{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Use focused stores.\"]}],\" Rather than one large general-purpose store, use smaller purpose-built stores: one per user, one for shared domain knowledge, and one for project-specific context. Each store has its own 10,000-memory limit, so keeping stores scoped reduces the chance any single one fills up.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Condense or prune before the store fills up.\"]}],\" Delete stale or redundant memories with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"memories.delete\"]}],\". You can also run a \",[\"$\",\"$L2d\",\"4\",{\"href\":\"/docs/en/managed-agents/dreams\",\"children\":[\"dreaming session\"]}],\", which consolidates fragmented content into a separate new output store rather than modifying the original. Switch your sessions over to that output store, then archive or delete the original.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Attach a new store when it makes sense.\"]}],\" If a store has grown beyond its useful scope, attach a fresh one for new content and attach the original with \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"read_only\"]}],\" access. The agent can read from both while only writing to the new one.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",\"7\",{\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",\"1\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",\"0\",{\"children\":[\"Limit write access where appropriate.\"]}],\" Sessions that only read shared reference material don't need \",[\"$\",\"code\",\"2\",{\"children\":[\"read_write\"]}],\". Keeping write access scoped to sessions that actually add new memories makes it easier to track where growth is coming from.\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n80:[\"$\",\"$L102\",null,{}]\n81:[\"$\",\"$L103\",null,{\"headings\":[{\"id\":\"overview\",\"text\":\"Overview\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"create-a-memory-store\",\"text\":\"Create a memory store\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"seed-it-with-content-optional\",\"text\":\"Seed it with content (optional)\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"attach-a-memory-store-to-a-session\",\"text\":\"Attach a memory store to a session\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"how-the-agent-accesses-memory\",\"text\":\"How the agent accesses memory\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"view-and-edit-memories\",\"text\":\"View and edit memories\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"list-memories\",\"text\":\"List memories\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"read-a-memory\",\"text\":\"Read a memory\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"create-a-memory\",\"text\":\"Create a memory\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"update-a-memory\",\"text\":\"Update a memory\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"delete-a-memory\",\"text\":\"Delete a memory\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"audit-memory-changes\",\"text\":\"Audit memory changes\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"list-versions\",\"text\":\"List versions\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"retrieve-a-version\",\"text\":\"Retrieve a version\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"redact-a-version\",\"text\":\"Redact a version\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"manage-memory-stores\",\"text\":\"Manage memory stores\",\"level\":2},{\"id\":\"list-stores\",\"text\":\"List stores\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"archive-a-store\",\"text\":\"Archive a store\",\"level\":3},{\"id\":\"best-practices-for-memory-management\",\"text\":\"Best practices for memory management\",\"level\":2}]}]\n82:[\"$\",\"$L104\",null,{\"headings\":\"$81:props:headings\",\"title\":\"Using agent memory\"}]\n83:[\"$\",\"$L105\",null,{}]\n106:T60b,\u003cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus\" style=\"--shiki-light:#1f2328;--shi